.Dd $Mdocdate: November 10 2026 $
.Dt IMAPIDLE.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imapidle.conf
.Nd imapidle configuration file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa ~/.config/imapidle/imapidle.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
tells
.Sy imapidle(1)
which IMAP accounts to watch and which
.Sy mbsync
channel to run when mail changes.
The file is INI.
One section is one account.
The section name is a label used in log lines.
The name
.Pa pulse
is reserved for channels that are not IMAP accounts.
See
.Sx PULSE CHANNELS .
.Pp
The directory should be mode 0700 and the file mode 0600.
A
.Va pass
value is stored in the file.
A
.Va pass_cmd
value is not a place to hide a secret: anyone who can read the file can
read the command.
.Pp
Lines that start with
.Ql #
or
.Ql ;
are comments.
Text after a value is not a comment.
.Pp
Each account requires
.Va server ,
.Va user ,
.Va mbsync_channel ,
and exactly one of
.Va pass
or
.Va pass_cmd .
A missing required key, both
.Va pass
and
.Va pass_cmd ,
a bad port, an empty
.Va folderN ,
or a bad
.Pa [pulse]
section
is written to standard error.
.Nm imapidle
then exits 1 and does not become a daemon.
A section with
.Va disabled
set to
.Cm yes
is kept and is not connected.
Required keys are not checked for that section.
Any other value leaves the section active.
The old names
.Va password
and
.Va password_cmd
are not accepted.
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width "mbsync_channel"
.It Va disabled
Set to
.Cm yes
to keep the section without connecting to it.
The comparison ignores case.
.It Va server
IMAP host name.
Required.
.It Va port
TCP port.
The default is 993.
.It Va user
IMAP login name.
Required.
.It Va pass
The IMAP password, used as-is.
Set this or
.Va pass_cmd ,
not both.
The value is not written to the log.
Required unless
.Va pass_cmd
is set.
.It Va pass_cmd
A command passed to
.Pa /bin/sh
with
.Fl c .
The first line of its standard output, without the trailing newline, is
the IMAP password.
The command must exit 0.
Empty output, a non-zero exit, or no exit within 30 seconds fails that
account only.
Required unless
.Va pass
is set.
The command is run again on each connection, so a helper that prints a
fresh access token can be dropped in here.
The command text and its output are not written to the log.
Standard error from the command is discarded.
.It Va auth
How
.Va pass ,
or the first line from
.Va pass_cmd ,
is presented to the server.
.Cm login
is the default and sends IMAP
.Cm LOGIN .
.Cm xoauth2
sends
.Cm AUTHENTICATE XOAUTH2 .
For
.Cm xoauth2
the value is a bearer token.
The token is not written to the log.
.It Va mbsync_channel
Channel name passed to
.Sy mbsync .
Required.
It must match a channel in the
.Sy mbsync
configuration.
.Nm imapidle
does not read that file.
.It Va wait
Seconds to sleep inside the
.Sy mbsync
child before exec.
The default is 0.
This does not stall the IMAP loop.
.It Va folder0 , folder1 , ...
Mailbox names, starting at
.Va folder0
with no gaps.
A value is either
.Ar name
or
.Ar name;priority=N .
Any other suffix is ignored.
A missing priority is 5.
.It Va folder
Used only when no
.Va folderN
key is present.
The default mailbox is
.Cm INBOX .
.It Va priority
Used only with
.Va folder ,
not with
.Va folderN .
The default is 5.
.El
.Pp
Every folder in a section shares that section's
.Va mbsync_channel ,
.Va user ,
and
.Va pass .
.Sh PRIORITY
Priority is the minimum time between
.Sy mbsync
runs for that folder:
.Bl -column "priority" "seconds" -offset indent
.It Sy priority Ta Sy seconds
.It 1 or less Ta 7
.It 2 Ta 42
.It 3 Ta 128
.It 4 Ta 256
.It 5 Ta 420
.It 6 Ta 540
.It 7 Ta 660
.It 8 Ta 780
.It 9 or more Ta 3600
.El
.Pp
A folder is ready when it has never been included in a run, or when the
minimum time since its last run has passed.
An event for a ready folder starts a 5 second wait on that
.Va mbsync_channel .
Events for other folders of the same channel during those 5 seconds join
one invocation, and do not start the 5 seconds over:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mbsync channel:INBOX channel:Archive
.Ed
.Pp
An event that arrives before the minimum time has passed is kept.
When the minimum time expires,
.Nm imapidle
schedules
.Sy mbsync
for that folder on the next wake.
That scheduling does not add another 5 seconds, unless the channel
already has a combine window open, in which case the folder joins it.
.Cm INBOX
at priority 5 is included in a run.
A further event for that mailbox during the next 420 seconds does not
start another run immediately.
At the end of those 420 seconds the folder is scheduled.
If no event arrives during those 420 seconds, the folder stays ready,
and the next event starts the 5 second wait.
.Pp
The
.Va wait
value is an extra delay inside the
.Sy mbsync
child, after the 5 second wait.
A batch uses the largest
.Va wait
among its folders.
.Sh PULSE CHANNELS
The optional
.Pa [pulse]
section names
.Sy mbsync
channels that are not IMAP accounts.
.Nm
runs each one as
.Pa mbsync channel
with no mailbox argument.
.Va channel0 ,
.Va channel1 ,
and so on start at 0 and have no gaps.
A channel name may not contain a space or a colon, and may not start
with a dash.
The same name twice is an error.
.Pp
.Va sweep
is how many seconds that channel waits after its own
.Sy mbsync
exits before it runs again.
The default is 3600.
Each channel keeps its own clock.
The first time the section is loaded, every channel is due and the
runs start together.
A run that takes longer starts its next wait later.
A channel that is still running is not started a second time.
The wait starts when that process exits.
.Pp
These runs do not pause IMAP, the 5 second combine window, or a
different channel.
The same channel does not overlap.
A bare
.Pa mbsync
of that channel and a
.Ar channel:box
run wait for each other.
.Pp
.Va disabled
set to
.Cm yes
holds the section.
.Va sweep
and
.Va channelN
are not checked while it is held.
Any other value leaves it active.
.Pp
On reload, a channel that remains keeps the clock it already has.
A channel that is new is due immediately.
A channel that was removed is not started again.
Changing
.Va sweep
applies the next time a run exits.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/imapidle/imapidle.conf
Default path.
.It Pa ~/.config/imapidle/known_hosts
SHA256 certificate fingerprints for this configuration's directory.
A current line is
.Pa server:port
and the fingerprint.
A retired line adds the GMT time it was replaced, as
.Ql YYYYMMDDTHH:MM:SSZ .
One line per host has no time.
.It Pa ~/.config/imapidle/learned
What each server did with
.Cm NOTIFY .
A line is
.Pa server:port ,
then
.Cm absent ,
.Cm rejected ,
or
.Cm active .
A rejected or active server may add the name it reported.
Delete a line to probe that server again.
The file mode is 0600 when
.Nm imapidle
creates it.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A password stored in the file, with a hot inbox and a lazy archive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[personal]
server = imap.example.com
port = 993
user = you@example.com
pass = secret
mbsync_channel = personal
folder0 = INBOX;priority=1
folder1 = Archive;priority=9
.Ed
.Pp
The same shape when a command prints the password.
.Sy pizauth show personal
is only an example of such a command:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[work]
server = imap.example.com
user = you@work.example
pass_cmd = pizauth show work
mbsync_channel = work
folder = INBOX
priority = 3
.Ed
.Pp
Channels that are not watched over IMAP:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[pulse]
sweep = 3600
channel0 = lists
channel1 = archive
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Sy imapidle(1)
